Let $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{d} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}.$
The projection of $\mathbf{v}$ onto $\mathbf{d}$ is
\begin{align*} \text{proj}_{\mathbf{d}} \mathbf{v} &= \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{d}}{\|\mathbf{d}\|^2} \mathbf{d} \\ &= \frac{\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}}{\left\| \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \right\|^2} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \frac{0(1) + 4(3)}{1^2 + 3^2} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \frac{12}{10} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \frac{6}{5} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 6/5 \\ 18/5 \end{pmatrix}. \end{align*}Then the reflection of $\mathbf{v}$ over the vector $\mathbf{d}$ is
\begin{align*} 2 \text{proj}_{\mathbf{d}} \mathbf{v} - \mathbf{v} &= 2 \begin{pmatrix} 6/5 \\ 18/5 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 12/5 \\ 36/5 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 20/5 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 12/5 \\ 16/5 \end{pmatrix}. \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 12/5 \\ 16/5 \end{pmatrix}}$

