Let $x = \cos 20^\circ.$  Then $3x - 4x^3 = \cos 60^\circ = \frac{1}{2},$ so $6x - 8x^3 = 1,$ which gives us $8x^3 - 6x + 1 = 0.$  Then $8x^3 - 6x - 1 = 0.$
Let $x = \cos 20^\circ.$ Then
\begin{align*} \cos 3 \theta &= 4 \cos^3 \theta - 3 \cos \theta \\ \cos 60^\circ &= 4 \cos^3 20^\circ - 3 \cos 20^\circ \\ \frac{1}{2} &= 4x^3 - 3x \\ 1 &= 8x^3 - 6x \\ 8x^3 - 6x - 1 &= 0 \end{align*}
Thus, the cubic polynomial is $8x^3 - 6x - 1.$

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{8x^3 - 6x - 1}$

