We have the conversion formulas
\begin{align*} x &= \rho \sin \phi \cos \theta \\ y &= \rho \sin \phi \sin \theta \\ z &= \rho \cos \phi \end{align*}
In our case, $\rho = 2$, $\theta = \pi$, and $\phi = \frac{\pi}{4}$. Then
\begin{align*} x &= 2 \sin \frac{\pi}{4} \cos \pi = 2 \left( \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \right) (-1) = -\sqrt{2} \\ y &= 2 \sin \frac{\pi}{4} \sin \pi = 2 \left( \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \right) (0) = 0 \\ z &= 2 \cos \frac{\pi}{4} = 2 \left( \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \right) = \sqrt{2} \end{align*}
Therefore, the rectangular coordinates are $(-\sqrt{2}, 0, \sqrt{2})$.

\boxed{(-\sqrt{2}, 0, \sqrt{2})}

