Let $\mathbf{A}$ and $\mathbf{B}$ be $2 \times 2$ matrices such that $\det \mathbf{A} = -1$ and $\det \mathbf{B} = 3.$  We want to find $\det (3 \mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}).$

We have
\begin{align*} \det (3 \mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}) &= \det (3 \mathbf{A}) \det (\mathbf{B}) \\ &= 3^2 \det (\mathbf{A}) \det (\mathbf{B}) \\ &= 9 \det (\mathbf{A}) \det (\mathbf{B}) \\ &= 9 (-1)(3) \\ &= -27. \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{-27}$

