Let $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}.$  Let $A$ be the matrix that corresponds to reflecting over the vector $\mathbf{v}.$  Then
\begin{align*} A &= \frac{1}{\|\mathbf{v}\|^2} \begin{pmatrix} v_1^2 - v_2^2 & 2v_1 v_2 \\ 2v_1 v_2 & v_2^2 - v_1^2 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \frac{1}{3^2 + 2^2} \begin{pmatrix} 3^2 - 2^2 & 2(3)(2) \\ 2(3)(2) & 2^2 - 3^2 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \frac{1}{13} \begin{pmatrix} 9 - 4 & 12 \\ 12 & 4 - 9 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \frac{1}{13} \begin{pmatrix} 5 & 12 \\ 12 & -5 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 5/13 & 12/13 \\ 12/13 & -5/13 \end{pmatrix}. \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 5/13 & 12/13 \\ 12/13 & -5/13 \end{pmatrix}}$

