Let $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}.$  Since $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are orthogonal, we can write $\mathbf{v} = \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{a}} \mathbf{v} + \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{v}.$  Then
\begin{align*} \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{v} &= \mathbf{v} - \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{a}} \mathbf{v} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{3}{5} \\ -\frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 3 - (-\frac{3}{5}) \\ -3 - (-\frac{6}{5}) \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 3 + \frac{3}{5} \\ -3 + \frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} \frac{15}{5} + \frac{3}{5} \\ -\frac{15}{5} + \frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} \frac{18}{5} \\ -\frac{9}{5} \end{pmatrix}. \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{18}{5} \\ -\frac{9}{5} \end{pmatrix}}$

