\begin{align*} 175_9 + 714_9 + 61_9 &= (1 \cdot 9^2 + 7 \cdot 9^1 + 5 \cdot 9^0) + (7 \cdot 9^2 + 1 \cdot 9^1 + 4 \cdot 9^0) + (6 \cdot 9^1 + 1 \cdot 9^0) \\ &= (81 + 63 + 5) + (63 + 9 + 4) + (54 + 1) \\ &= 149 + 76 + 55 \\ &= 280 \end{align*}
Now we convert $280$ to base $9$.
\begin{align*} 280 \div 9 &= 31 \text{ R } 1 \\ 31 \div 9 &= 3 \text{ R } 4 \\ 3 \div 9 &= 0 \text{ R } 3 \end{align*}
So $280 = 341_9$.

Alternatively, we can add directly in base 9.
\begin{array}{@{}c@{\,}c@{}c@{}c} & 1 & 7 & 5_9 \\ & 7 & 1 & 4_9 \\ + & & 6 & 1_9 \\ \hline \end{array}
$5+4+1 = 10 = 1 \cdot 9 + 1$, so we write down 1 and carry-over 1.
\begin{array}{@{}c@{\,}c@{}c@{}c} & 1 & \stackrel{1}{7} & 5_9 \\ & 7 & 1 & 4_9 \\ + & & 6 & 1_9 \\ \hline & & & 1_9 \end{array}
$1+7+1+6 = 15 = 1 \cdot 9 + 6$, so we write down 6 and carry-over 1.
\begin{array}{@{}c@{\,}c@{}c@{}c} & \stackrel{1}{1} & \stackrel{1}{7} & 5_9 \\ & 7 & 1 & 4_9 \\ + & & 6 & 1_9 \\ \hline & & 6 & 1_9 \end{array}
$1+1+7 = 9 = 1 \cdot 9 + 0$, so we write down 0 and carry-over 1.
\begin{array}{@{}c@{\,}c@{}c@{}c} & \stackrel{1}{1} & \stackrel{1}{7} & 5_9 \\ & 7 & 1 & 4_9 \\ + & & 6 & 1_9 \\ \hline & 1 & 0 & 6 & 1_9 \end{array}
Therefore, $175_9 + 714_9 + 61_9 = 1061_9$.

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{1061_9}$

