Let the normal vector to the plane $2x + y - 2z + 3 = 0$ be $\mathbf{n}_1 = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}.$  Let the normal vector to the plane $6x + 3y + 2z - 5 = 0$ be $\mathbf{n}_2 = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 3 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}.$  Then
\begin{align*} \cos \theta &= \frac{|\mathbf{n}_1 \cdot \mathbf{n}_2|}{\|\mathbf{n}_1\| \|\mathbf{n}_2\|} \\ &= \frac{|(2)(6) + (1)(3) + (-2)(2)|}{\sqrt{2^2 + 1^2 + (-2)^2} \sqrt{6^2 + 3^2 + 2^2}} \\ &= \frac{|12 + 3 - 4|}{\sqrt{4 + 1 + 4} \sqrt{36 + 9 + 4}} \\ &= \frac{|11|}{\sqrt{9} \sqrt{49}} \\ &= \frac{11}{3 \cdot 7} \\ &= \frac{11}{21}. \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{\frac{11}{21}}$

