Let $A = 4-3i$, $M = -4+i$, $S = i$, and $P = 2$. We want to find $A-M+S-P$.
We have
\begin{align*} A-M+S-P &= (4-3i) - (-4+i) + i - 2 \\ &= 4 - 3i + 4 - i + i - 2 \\ &= (4+4-2) + (-3i - i + i) \\ &= 6 - 3i\end{aligned}
Therefore, $A-M+S-P = 6-3i$.

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{6-3i}$

