Let $z$ be a complex number. We want to find the minimum value of $|z + 5 - 3i| + |z - 7 + 2i|$. We can interpret $|z + 5 - 3i|$ as the distance between the complex number $z$ and the complex number $-5 + 3i$, and $|z - 7 + 2i|$ as the distance between the complex number $z$ and the complex number $7 - 2i$. Thus, we want to minimize the sum of the distances from $z$ to $-5 + 3i$ and $7 - 2i$.

Let $A = -5 + 3i$ and $B = 7 - 2i$. Then we want to minimize $|z - A| + |z - B|$. This is minimized when $z$ lies on the line segment connecting $A$ and $B$. In this case, the minimum value is the distance between $A$ and $B$, which is
\begin{align*} |A - B| &= |(-5 + 3i) - (7 - 2i)| \\ &= |-5 + 3i - 7 + 2i| \\ &= |-12 + 5i| \\ &= \sqrt{(-12)^2 + 5^2} \\ &= \sqrt{144 + 25} \\ &= \sqrt{169} \\ &= 13. \end{align*}

Thus, the minimum value of $|z + 5 - 3i| + |z - 7 + 2i|$ is 13.

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{13}$

