Let the given equation be $x^2 - 2x - 1 = 0$.
Since $\alpha$ and $\beta$ are the roots, we have $\alpha + \beta = 2$ and $\alpha \beta = -1$.
Also, $\alpha^2 - 2 \alpha - 1 = 0$ and $\beta^2 - 2 \beta - 1 = 0$, which implies $\alpha^2 = 2 \alpha + 1$ and $\beta^2 = 2 \beta + 1$.
Then
\begin{align*} \alpha^3 &= \alpha (2 \alpha + 1) = 2 \alpha^2 + \alpha = 2(2 \alpha + 1) + \alpha = 4 \alpha + 2 + \alpha = 5 \alpha + 2 \\ \alpha^4 &= \alpha (5 \alpha + 2) = 5 \alpha^2 + 2 \alpha = 5(2 \alpha + 1) + 2 \alpha = 10 \alpha + 5 + 2 \alpha = 12 \alpha + 5 \end{align*}
and
\begin{align*} \beta^3 &= \beta (2 \beta + 1) = 2 \beta^2 + \beta = 2(2 \beta + 1) + \beta = 4 \beta + 2 + \beta = 5 \beta + 2 \end{align*}
Therefore,
\begin{align*} 5 \alpha^4 + 12 \beta^3 &= 5 (12 \alpha + 5) + 12 (5 \beta + 2) \\ &= 60 \alpha + 25 + 60 \beta + 24 \\ &= 60 (\alpha + \beta) + 49 \\ &= 60 (2) + 49 \\ &= 120 + 49 \\ &= 169 \end{align*}

Thus, $5 \alpha^4 + 12 \beta^3 = 169$.

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{169}$

