Let $G_n = F_{3n}$. We are given that $G_n = a G_{n-1} + b G_{n-2}$ for every integer $n \ge 2$.
We have $G_0 = F_0 = 0$, $G_1 = F_3 = 2$, $G_2 = F_6 = 8$, $G_3 = F_9 = 34$, $G_4 = F_{12} = 144$, $G_5 = F_{15} = 610$.
Using the recurrence relation $G_n = a G_{n-1} + b G_{n-2}$, we can write
\begin{align*} G_2 &= a G_1 + b G_0 \\ 8 &= a(2) + b(0) \\ 8 &= 2a \\ a &= 4 \end{align*}
\begin{align*} G_3 &= a G_2 + b G_1 \\ 34 &= 4(8) + b(2) \\ 34 &= 32 + 2b \\ 2 &= 2b \\ b &= 1 \end{align*}
\begin{align*} G_4 &= a G_3 + b G_2 \\ 144 &= 4(34) + 1(8) \\ 144 &= 136 + 8 \\ 144 &= 144 \end{align*}
\begin{align*} G_5 &= a G_4 + b G_3 \\ 610 &= 4(144) + 1(34) \\ 610 &= 576 + 34 \\ 610 &= 610 \end{align*}
Thus, we have $a = 4$ and $b = 1$.

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{(4,1)}$

