Let $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 13 \end{pmatrix}.$  We are given that $\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{a}} \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}.$  Since $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are orthogonal, we can write $\mathbf{v} = \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{a}} \mathbf{v} + \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{v}.$  Therefore,
\begin{align*} \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{v} &= \mathbf{v} - \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{a}} \mathbf{v} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 13 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ 9 \end{pmatrix}. \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ 9 \end{pmatrix}}$

