We first complete the square to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form.
\begin{align*} x^2 - 6x - 4y^2 - 8y &= 27 \\ (x^2 - 6x) - 4(y^2 + 2y) &= 27 \\ (x^2 - 6x + 9) - 4(y^2 + 2y + 1) &= 27 + 9 - 4(1) \\ (x-3)^2 - 4(y+1)^2 &= 32 \\ \frac{(x-3)^2}{32} - \frac{(y+1)^2}{8} &= 1 \end{align*}
The center of the hyperbola is $(3, -1).$ Here, $a^2 = 32$ and $b^2 = 8.$ Then $c^2 = a^2 + b^2 = 32 + 8 = 40,$ so $c = \sqrt{40} = 2 \sqrt{10}.$ The distance between the foci is $2c = 2(2 \sqrt{10}) = 4 \sqrt{10}.$

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{4 \sqrt{10}}$

