Let $a$ and $b$ be complex numbers such that $a \overline{b} = -1 + 5i.$ We want to find $\overline{a} b.$

We have
\begin{align*} \overline{a \overline{b}} &= \overline{-1 + 5i} \\ \overline{a} \overline{\overline{b}} &= -1 - 5i \\ \overline{a} b &= -1 - 5i. \end{align*}

Thus, $\overline{a} b = -1 - 5i.$

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{-1 - 5i}$

