Let $t = \tan \frac{x}{2}.$ Then $\sin x = \frac{2t}{1 + t^2}$ and $\cos x = \frac{1 - t^2}{1 + t^2}.$ Thus,
\begin{align*} \frac{1 + \sin x - \cos x}{1 + \sin x + \cos x} &= \frac{1 + \frac{2t}{1 + t^2} - \frac{1 - t^2}{1 + t^2}}{1 + \frac{2t}{1 + t^2} + \frac{1 - t^2}{1 + t^2}} \\ &= \frac{(1 + t^2) + 2t - (1 - t^2)}{(1 + t^2) + 2t + (1 - t^2)} \\ &= \frac{1 + t^2 + 2t - 1 + t^2}{1 + t^2 + 2t + 1 - t^2} \\ &= \frac{2t^2 + 2t}{2 + 2t} \\ &= \frac{2t(t + 1)}{2(1 + t)} \\ &= t \\ &= \tan \frac{x}{2}. \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{\tan \frac{x}{2}}$

